{title: 039 - Lord, in the Morning}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #039 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 39}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Lord, in [C]the [F]morning [Dm]Thou shalt [C]hear
[C]My [F]voice ascending high;
[C]To [F]Thee [Dm]will [Bb]I [F]direct [Dm]my [C]prayer,
[F]To Thee [Bb]lift [C7]up mine [F]eye—
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Up to [C]the [F]hills [Dm]where Christ is [C]gone
[C]To [F]plead for [Gm]all [C]His [F]saints,
[C]Presenting [Bb]at [F]His [C]Father's throne
[F]Our songs [Bb]and [C7]our complaints.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]O may [C]Thy [F]Spirit [Dm]guide my [C]feet
[C]In [F]ways of [Gm]righteousness;
[C]Make every [Bb]path [F]of [C]duty straight
[F]And plain [Bb]before [C7]my [F]face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]The men [C]that [F]love [Dm]and fear Thy [C]name
[C]Shall [F]see their [C/G]hopes fulfilled;
[C]The [F]mighty [Bb]God [F]will [C]compass them
[F]With favor [C7]as a [F]shield.
{end_of_verse}
